    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Normalize one audio or video segment to a target loudness.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --target-loudness TEXT \r\n                              Target integrated loudness in LUFS (default -14)\r\n          --average-loudness TEXT \r\n                              Pre-measured integrated loudness in LUFS; must be used with\r\n                              --peak-loudness\r\n          --peak-loudness TEXT \r\n                              Pre-measured SDK loudness-detector peak; must be used with\r\n                              --average-loudness\r\n          --true-peak-ceiling TEXT \r\n                              Optional output true-peak ceiling in dBTP; measured from source\r\n                              audio and enforced by reducing the target\r\n          --enable TEXT       Enable or disable loudness normalization: true / false (default\r\n                              true)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Detect the selected source window and normalize it to -14 LUFS\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --seg-id <UUID> --target-loudness -14\r\n  # Keep the measured output True Peak at or below -1 dBTP\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --seg-id <UUID> --target-loudness -14 --true-peak-ceiling -1\r\n  # Reuse pre-measured values instead of running detection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --average-loudness -20.3 \\\r\n      --peak-loudness -1.2 --target-loudness -14 --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Disable loudness normalization on the selected segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --seg-id <UUID> --enable false\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --average-loudness and --peak-loudness must be passed together.\r\n  - --true-peak-ceiling measures source True Peak (dBTP) and lowers the effective target when necessary.\r\n  - Ceiling mode still measures True Peak even with explicit --average-loudness/--peak-loudness.\r\n  - Without explicit measurements, the command analyzes the segment's source time range.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Normalize one audio or video segment to a target loudness.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --target-loudness TEXT \r\n                              Target integrated loudness in LUFS (default -14)\r\n          --average-loudness TEXT \r\n                              Pre-measured integrated loudness in LUFS; must be used with\r\n                              --peak-loudness\r\n          --peak-loudness TEXT \r\n                              Pre-measured SDK loudness-detector peak; must be used with\r\n                              --average-loudness\r\n          --true-peak-ceiling TEXT \r\n                              Optional output true-peak ceiling in dBTP; measured from source\r\n                              audio and enforced by reducing the target\r\n          --enable TEXT       Enable or disable loudness normalization: true / false (default\r\n                              true)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Detect the selected source window and normalize it to -14 LUFS\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --seg-id <UUID> --target-loudness -14\r\n  # Keep the measured output True Peak at or below -1 dBTP\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --seg-id <UUID> --target-loudness -14 --true-peak-ceiling -1\r\n  # Reuse pre-measured values instead of running detection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --average-loudness -20.3 \\\r\n      --peak-loudness -1.2 --target-loudness -14 --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Disable loudness normalization on the selected segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo loudness-normalize --seg-id <UUID> --enable false\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --average-loudness and --peak-loudness must be passed together.\r\n  - --true-peak-ceiling measures source True Peak (dBTP) and lowers the effective target when necessary.\r\n  - Ceiling mode still measures True Peak even with explicit --average-loudness/--peak-loudness.\r\n  - Without explicit measurements, the command analyzes the segment's source time range.\r\n",
